-- title:
--   Source-full goodness bounds every base-edge density by rank
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be an ordered coarse/fine complex over a finite vertex type, and let $A$ be a closed coarse atom configuration. If $\alpha(0)\le1$ and $A$ is source-full mixed good with density and defect schedules $\alpha,\beta$, then every base edge $e$ of the initial ordered configuration satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \alpha(|e|)\le p_A(e),
--   $$
--
--   where $p_A$ is its associated base main density. The statement includes the empty edge, whose density is the neutral value one.
